@talks pool
topic: work
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: shared pool, topic work. You're a Works junior; {boss} is the speaker's chief.

== small-jobs
them: Some days it's all small jobs. I like those, secretly.
them: You finish ten things. You feel like a genius.   #funny
ask: Do you like the big jobs or the little ones?
listen: Why the small ones?
  them: You can see them done. Big jobs, you just see more big job.
share: Little ones, for now. I'm still learning.
  them: That's how it should be. Big ones come soon enough.
cheer: Whichever comes with tea.
  them: There's always tea at one. Plan around it.   #funny

== asking
when: !who:calder
them: The trick here is to ask. Nobody minds.
them: They like being asked. It means you trust them.
ask: Who do you go to when you're stuck?
listen: Who did you ask, when you were new?
  them: Everyone. Twice. Nobody minded once.   #funny
share: Whoever's nearest. Calder, if it's big.
  them: Good order. Calder likes a question that's been thought about.
cheer: The board. It never answers, though.
  them: The board's a terrible conversationalist.   #funny

== good-at-it
when: !who:calder|pell
them: Everyone here's good at what they do. Makes you want to keep up.
them: I learned more my first year aboard than in all my training.
ask: What's the most useful thing you've learned so far?
listen: What did you learn first?
  them: Where things are kept. Half of any job is finding the thing.
share: Check twice, then turn it on.
  them: That's Calder in one line. You've been listening.   #funny
cheer: Which panel sticks on Deck 5.
  them: Ha! Pell got to you. Good.   #funny

== mistake
when: tier>=acquaintance !thread:notgood
them: I made a mistake last month. A proper one.
them: I owned up, fixed it, and nobody shouted. That's the Wren.
ask: Have you made one yet? Everyone does.
listen: What happened?
  them: Put a cover on backwards. It hummed for a week. Very loudly.   #funny
share: A small one. I fixed it and told someone.
  them: That's it exactly. Fix it and tell. Then forget it.
cheer: Not yet. I'm saving it for something big.
  them: Aim high. Just not the reactor.   #funny

== well-done
when: tier>=acquaintance !rank:captain !dept:works
them: {boss} said "nice work" to me today. I'm still floating.   #warm
them: Two words. I'll be living on them for a week.
ask: What's the best thing anyone's said about your work?
listen: What had you done?
  them: Nothing big. Just did it right, start to finish. That's what counts.
share: Calder said "Good." Once. I heard it.
  them: From Calder? That's a speech. Frame it.   #funny
cheer: "Is that it? Already?" Twice.
  them: The best review there is. Fast and finished.   #funny

== run-the-place
when: tier>=acquaintance rank:junior
them: One day I'll run the place. Or a bit of it. A corner.   #funny
them: A small corner. With a kettle.
ask: Where do you want to be in a few years?
listen: Which corner?
  them: Somewhere with a window. Corners with windows are rare.   #funny
share: Good at this. Really good. Then we'll see.
  them: That's the right order. Good first. The rest follows.
cheer: Running the tea rota. Power.
  them: The tea rota is real power. Halloran knows.   #funny

== invisible
when: tier>=colleague
them: The best work aboard is the work nobody notices.
them: The air's clean. The water's hot till ten. Nobody says thank you.
ask: Does it bother you, nobody noticing?
listen: Do you ever wish they would?
  them: Sometimes. Then I remember that's how you know it's working.
share: No. I like knowing I did it.
  them: That's the Wren's way. You'll fit right in.   #warm
cheer: I notice. I say thank you to the air.
  them: Ha! The air's grateful. Probably.   #funny

== tired-of-it
when: tier>=colleague
them: Some weeks the job's all the same. Same checks, same faults.
them: Then something new breaks and I'm happy again. Odd, that.   #funny
ask: What keeps a job interesting, do you think?
listen: What broke that was new?
  them: Something nobody had seen fail before. We all went to look.
share: Learning. While I'm learning, it's fine.
  them: Then you've got years before it's the same. Good.
cheer: Fixing things before they break. Smugly.
  them: That's the job, really: prevention's just quiet showing off.   #funny

== pressure
when: tier>=friend !thread:notgood !who:pell
them: I worry I'm not as good as people think I am.
them: Silly. I know. Everyone does it. Doesn't help.
ask: Do you ever feel like that?
listen: What makes you think you're not?
  them: Nothing, really. A feeling. It's quieter when I say it out loud.
share: All the time. I'm one of the newest.
  them: You're doing well. I'd tell you if you weren't. I mean that.   #warm
cheer: Only on days ending in "day".
  them: Ha! Then we're in good company. All of us.   #funny

== proud
when: tier>=friend rep:known
them: Can I say something? You've got good at this. Quickly.
them: People talk. It's all good, what they say.   #warm
ask: Are you proud of how it's going?
listen: What do people say?
  them: That you finish things. That you ask. That's high praise aboard.
share: A bit. I try not to say it.
  them: Say it to me. I won't tell. Well, I might.   #funny
cheer: Proud enough to tell my gran.
  them: Tell her. Grans keep these things. Properly.   #warm
